\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The royal banners forward go;
\par The Cross shines forth in mystic glow;
\par Where He in flesh, our flesh who made,
\par Our sentence bore, our ransom paid:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Where deep for us the spear was dyed,
\par Life's torrent rushing from His side 
\par To wash us in that precios flood,
\par Where mingled water flowed, and blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Fulfilled is all that David told
\par In true prophetic song of old:
\par Amidst the nations, God, saith he,
\par Hath reigned and triumphed from the tree.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O Tree of beauty, Tree of light!
\par O Tree with royal purple dight!
\par Elect on whose triumphal breast
\par Those holy limbs should find their rest:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. On whose dear arms, so widely flung,
\par The weight of this world's ransom hung:
\par The price of humankind to pay,
\par And spoil the spoiler of his prey.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. To Thee, eternal Three in One,
\par Let homage meet by all be done:
\par Whom by the Cross Thou dost restore,
\par Preserve and govern evermore.
\par                                     Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

